<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.75%" pitch="-2.60%">
      The Lord is merciful and gracious.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Slow to anger and abounding in steadfast love.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Slow to anger.<break time="500ms"/>
      Think about that for a moment.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not quick to react.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not easily provoked.<break time="500ms"/>
      But patient, deeply patient, with a patience that outlasts every failure you bring to Him.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He will not always chide, nor will he keep his anger forever.<break time="1000ms"/>
      His correction is not permanent.<break time="500ms"/>
      His displeasure does not define the relationship.<break time="500ms"/>
      It passes, like weather, while His love remains like the ground beneath.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He does not deal with us according to our sins.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Nor repay us according to our iniquities.<break time="1800ms"/>

      If God kept a ledger, none of us could stand.<break time="500ms"/>
      But the psalm tells us He does not operate that way.<break time="500ms"/>
      He is not tallying your wrongs.<break time="500ms"/>
      He is not measuring your worth by your worst day.<break time="1000ms"/>
      His patience is vast.<break time="1800ms"/>

      There is a kind of love that keeps score.<break time="500ms"/>
      And there is a kind of love that keeps showing up.<break time="500ms"/>
      God's love is the second kind.<break time="1000ms"/>
      It does not depend on your performance.<break time="500ms"/>
      It does not waver with your mood.<break time="500ms"/>
      It abounds.<break time="1000ms"/>
      That word means it overflows.<break time="500ms"/>
      There is always more than enough.<break time="1800ms"/>

      You do not have to earn what He freely gives.<break time="500ms"/>
      His mercy is great.<break time="1000ms"/>
      His love is everlasting.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
